 ## Background
-The RaySamples structure is part of modern neural rendering frameworks that combine explicit geometry (SDFs, Gaussians) with implicit neural representations [S1, unofficial]. It enables the integration of LiDAR data with visual rendering by providing a common data format for ray-sample interactions [S1, unofficial]. The specific implementation with `pred_xyz`, `pred_sdf`, and `pred_isigma` fields is characteristic of systems like GS-SDF, which unify Gaussian Splatting and SDF-based reconstruction [S1, unofficial]. The optical sampling model described in [S2, unofficial] originates from computational photography and gradient optics, applying physical lens models to neural rendering.
